     "text": "{\"reachable\": true, \"rationale\": \"Blocking h3_1:obtain does not cut every path to the target. Both entry footholds give h1_0:reach (from edge0), h1_1:obtain and h1_2:traverse. Those make h2_1:access (AND of edge0, h1_1, h1_0) and h2_2:obtain (from h1_2). h3_0:reach is then reachable, since all its parents (h1_2, h2_1, h2_2) are reached. h3_0 makes h5_0:reach (OR) reachable, and h5_0 makes crown:obtain (OR) reachable. Other routes also work, for example via h2_0, h3_2, h4_0 and h5_1.\"}"
